-- title:
--   Igusa degree equality for Γ₁(L)≤Γ≤Γ₀(L)
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field, let $L$ be a non-zero natural number whose image in $K$ is non-zero, and let $\Gamma$ be a subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ with $\Gamma_1(L)\le\Gamma\le\Gamma_0(L)$. Consider the intermediate field [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC K Γ`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101) of the Laurent series field $K((q))$, namely the subfield generated over $K$ by all quotients $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,K\,p_f/\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,K\,p_g$, where $f,g$ are modular forms of one and the same weight $k$ for the image of $\Gamma$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$, $p_f,p_g$ are power series over $\mathbb{Z}$ satisfying the predicates `IsIntegralQExp f pf` and `IsIntegralQExp g pg` (integral $q$-expansions at $\infty$ of $f$ and of $g$), and the Laurent series over $K$ attached to $p_g$ is non-zero. Let $x$ be an element of this field whose underlying Laurent series is [`ModularCurve.jqModC K`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L15), that is $q^{-1}$ times the image in $K[[q]]$ of the integral power series `jNum` $=E_4^3\cdot(\text{inverse Dedekind eta unit})$, the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant $j$. Then the degree of [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC K Γ`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101) over the subfield $K(x)$ generated by $x$ over $K$ is finite and equals the index in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ of the subgroup generated by $\Gamma$ together with $-I$.
--
--   This is Igusa's degree theorem in the equality form: the field cut out in $K((q))$ by reductions of integral $q$-expansions at the single cusp $\infty$, for a level structure between $\Gamma_1(L)$ and $\Gamma_0(L)$ and in characteristic not dividing $L$, has exactly the generic degree $[\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}):\pm\Gamma]$ over the $j$-line. It combines the generic upper bound (applied to $\Gamma\cdot\{\pm 1\}$) with a lower bound obtained in moduli form from torsion orbits on elliptic curves with transcendental $j$-invariant, and is used downstream in the characterisations of membership in the Igusa–Gauss ring for $q$-expansions at full level.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_finrank_adjoin_jqModC_qExpFunctionFieldC_eq_index_of_gamma1_le_of_le_gamma0.lean

